# Deployment and operations context.

```yaml
deploymentContext:
  deployment:
    cloudProvider: AWS
    ci:
      provider: github-actions
      prChecks:
        - pytest
        - Docker image build
        - Container health smoke test
      watchCommand: "gh pr checks --watch"
    environments:
      - name: local
        deployMechanism: docker-compose
        runCommand: "docker compose up -d"
      - name: production
        deployMechanism: GitHub Actions SSH to Ubuntu EC2
        runCommand: "bash scripts/deploy.sh"
    strategy:
      type: rolling-replacement-single-host
      featureFlags: none
    rollback:
      code: "Retain the pre-deployment image ID locally; if the new container fails its health check, replace it with a container started from that previous image."
      limitations:
        - A first deployment has no previous image to restore.
        - Single-host replacement causes a brief restart window.
    observability:
      apm: TBD
      logs: Docker container logs and GitHub Actions logs
      healthEndpoint: /health
    network:
      publicPorts:
        - "80/tcp"
      restrictedPorts:
        - "22/tcp from administrator IP only"
      privateContainerPorts:
        - "5000/tcp"
```
